Burnoff
=======

Sentinel-2 SWIR flare detection at LNG facilities.


Requirements
------------

- Python 3.12+ with uv
- tippecanoe (for PMTiles)
- Node.js (for npx serve)


Quick Start
-----------

    make all        # Run full pipeline
    make serve      # Start web server on :8000


Detection
---------

Single location:

    uv run burnoff detect --lat -12.51 --lon 130.92 --year 2025

Bulk processing:

    uv run burnoff bulk terminals.json -o detections.json --year 2025


Algorithm
---------

Per-pixel detection using Sentinel-2 L2A bands:
- Intensity: B12 > 0.3, B11 > 0.2
- Contrast: B12 > 3× local median
- Thermal: (B11 - B8A) / (B11 + B8A) > 0

Cross-date clustering merges detections whose circular footprints overlap:
- radius = sqrt(pixels / π) × 20m
- merge if distance ≤ max(50m, radius_a + radius_b)


Data Sources
------------

- Sentinel-2 L2A via Element84 STAC API
- SWIR bands: B11 (1610nm), B12 (2190nm)
- Scene classification (SCL) for cloud masking
